From a711d4330e7fa00d3ffa8529c97679fce6071cd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AegisOS Build <build@aegisos.local>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 22:09:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 39/89] aegisos: initialize ExternalStorageService component on
 any user's unlock

StorageSessionController#onUnlockUser() only called
initExternalStorageServiceComponent() when userId == 0, even though the
component it resolves (MediaProvider's ExternalStorageService binding
target) is global, identical for every user. On stock Android this is
harmless -- user 0 always unlocks first -- but under Duress Unlock's
decoy switch, user 0 may never unlock this boot at all, so the
component name stays permanently null and no user's storage session
(including the decoy's own) can ever bind to it:
StorageUserConnection.connectIfNeeded() throws "Not ready to bind" for
every subsequent user, confirmed via logcat as the actual proximate
cause of the "Volume external_primary not found" crash the earlier
StorageManagerService#getVolumeList() fix (0038) did not resolve.

Guard on whether the component is already resolved instead of which
user triggered the check -- same one-time-init outcome for every
existing Android flow, but now also correct when the decoy is the first
user to ever unlock.
---
 .../server/storage/StorageSessionController.java       | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/storage/StorageSessionController.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/storage/StorageSessionController.java
index 0a1271611c8a..3afe579bb0d0 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/storage/StorageSessionController.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/storage/StorageSessionController.java
@@ -272,7 +272,15 @@ public final class StorageSessionController {
      */
     public void onUnlockUser(int userId) throws ExternalStorageServiceException {
         Slog.i(TAG, "On user unlock " + userId);
-        if (userId == 0) {
+        // mExternalStorageServiceComponent resolves a single, global component name (identical
+        // for every user, not per-user data), so this only needs to run once -- gating on
+        // "userId == 0" instead of "not yet initialized" assumed user 0 always unlocks first,
+        // true on stock Android but not under AegisOS Duress Unlock, where a decoy switch must
+        // succeed even when user 0 has never unlocked this boot. With the old check, no user's
+        // storage session (including the decoy's own) could ever bind to the
+        // ExternalStorageService: StorageUserConnection.connectIfNeeded() throws "Not ready to
+        // bind" whenever getExternalStorageServiceComponentName() is still null.
+        if (mExternalStorageServiceComponent == null) {
             initExternalStorageServiceComponent();
         }
     }
